76,13173,5302,429,279,26313,315,279,12804,315,264,47311,17767,282,2075,8,1124,8,553,17767,856,481,272,1124,8,374,17767,282,1337,8,1124,568,758,419,1142,11,582,525,49702,553,17767,856,488,220,20,1124,701,892,646,387,5326,438,17767,856,481,10293,20,8,1124,701,773,17767,272,284,481,20,1124,3593,22043,279,47311,17767,282,2075,8,284,595,87,61,19,488,220,24,87,61,18,488,595,87,61,17,488,220,18,17,87,481,220,16,16,1124,701,582,1184,311,1477,279,897,315,17767,595,1124,8,1741,429,279,26313,979,17767,282,2075,8,1124,8,374,17779,553,17767,856,488,220,20,1124,8,374,220,19,13,10548,311,279,91592,1107,576,13173,11,419,3363,17767,282,4080,20,8,284,220,19,1124,3593,5338,11,582,27679,17767,856,284,481,20,1124,8,1119,279,47311,17767,282,2075,8,1124,7731,59,9640,69,4080,20,8,284,595,4080,20,29776,19,488,220,24,4080,20,29776,18,488,595,4080,20,29776,17,488,220,18,17,4080,20,8,481,220,16,16,198,59,21675,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,23526,504,279,74003,13,9258,1172,279,41171,13,3155,537,17024,279,6291,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe remainder when $kx^4+9x^3+kx^2+32x-11$ is divided by $x + 5$ is $4$.  Find $k.$\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo solve the problem, we will use the Remainder Theorem. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of a polynomial \\( f(x) \\) by \\( x - c \\) is \\( f(c) \\). In this case, we are dividing by \\( x + 5 \\), which can be written as \\( x - (-5) \\), so \\( c = -5 \\).\n\nGiven the polynomial \\( f(x) = kx^4 + 9x^3 + kx^2 + 32x - 11 \\), we need to find the value of \\( k \\) such that the remainder when \\( f(x) \\) is divided by \\( x + 5 \\) is 4. According to the Remainder Theorem, this means \\( f(-5) = 4 \\).\n\nFirst, we substitute \\( x = -5 \\) into the polynomial \\( f(x) \\):\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = k(-5)^4 + 9(-5)^3 + k(-5)^2 + 32(-5) - 11\n\\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"a47fb9e74a337c5f7db4aceee41b6726e3b999b9f8d905a4e980882517d88495"},"seconds":16.76077699661255,"seed":326481407098253687,"stop":"eos","text":"\\[\nf(-5) = k(-5)^4 + 9(-5)^3 + k(-5)^2 + 32(-5) - 11\n\\]\n\nSimplify each term:\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = k(625) + 9(-125) + k(25) + 32(-5) - 11\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = 625k - 1125 + 25k - 160 - 11\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = 650k - 1296\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\( f(-5) = 4 \\) according to the problem statement:\n\n\\[\n650k - 1296 = 4\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\( k \\):\n\n\\[\n650k = 4 + 1296\n\\]\n\n\\[\n650k = 1300\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{1300}{650}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"\\[\nf(-5) = k(-5)^4 + 9(-5)^3 + k(-5)^2 + 32(-5) - 11\n\\]\n\nSimplify each term:\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = k(625) + 9(-125) + k(25) + 32(-5) - 11\n\\]\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = 625k - 1125 + 25k - 160 - 11\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\nf(-5) = 650k - 1296\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\( f(-5) = 4 \\) according to the problem statement:\n\n\\[\n650k - 1296 = 4\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\( k \\):\n\n\\[\n650k = 4 + 1296\n\\]\n\n\\[\n650k = 1300\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{1300}{650}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).","id":"intermediate_algebra:583"}
